their outputs logically linked anyway, and the essay's operational edge rule suggests they don't, but I'm still weighing that.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether defecting is the dominant choice under A-FDT, since the other copy's action seems to depend only on its own input. But I'm wondering if treating the two copies as logically linked, with the input difference irrelevant, changes that conclusion.\n\nUnder A-FDT, send beats quiet by a fixed margin whatever the probability s, so dominance points to defecting. The open question is whether the two copies' differing inputs make their outputs logically linked anyway, and the essay's operational edge rule suggests they don't, but I'm still weighing that.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10047,"completion_tokens":1033,"total_tokens":11080,"cost":0.060848,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.060848,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040188,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02066},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":616,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}